# Suspension is itself a decision (sections IV and X) {isGroup: true}

<Suspension is itself a passional decision>: Refusing to decide a genuine option is not a way of avoiding passional decision; it is one more passional decision, with the same risk of losing truth. {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "pp. 11, 26-27"}

(1) [Not deciding is itself a passional decision]: "to say, under such circumstances," 'Do not decide, but leave the question open,' "is itself a passional decision,---just like deciding yes or no,---and is attended with the same risk of losing the truth" {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 11", note: "One sentence of the source; the inner quoted words are James's, split here only because the converter escapes the inner quotation marks.", about: [{stance: wait, passional: yes}, {stance: believe, passional: yes}], causes: {from: suspend, to: truth, sign: "-", on: chance, basis: asserted, chain: risk}}
