[Waiting means acting as if religion were not true]: The command that we "wait---acting of course meanwhile more or less as if religion were not true" {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 29", note: "Footnote 4: 'he who forbids us to believe religion to be true, necessarily also forbids us to act as we should if we did believe it to be true.'", causes: {from: veto, to: suspend, sign: "+", basis: asserted, chain: religion}}

