<Religion is a genuine option>: For those to whom it is live, the religious hypothesis is a momentous and forced option that the intellect cannot settle. {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "pp. 25-27"}

(1) [Genuine option]
(2) [Live hypothesis]
(3) [Religion's first affirmation]: Religion "says that the best things are the more eternal things, the overlapping things, the things in the universe that throw the last stone, so to speak, and say the final word." {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 25", note: "Charles Secretan's phrase 'Perfection is eternal'; 'an affirmation which obviously cannot yet be verified scientifically at all'."}
