[The freedom to believe licenses patent superstition]: Some hearers "shrink from radically saying" that "we have the right to believe at our own risk any hypothesis that is live enough to tempt our will" because they apply the freedom "to the case of some patent superstition", faith being "when you believe something that you know ain't true." #contested {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 29"}
